# Local E2E overrides — copy to `.env.test.local` (gitignored) to run the e2e
# suite against a local server with NO deploy. Values here override the
# committed staging defaults in `.env.test`; a shell env var overrides both.
#
#   cp .env.test.local.example .env.test.local
#   npm run test:e2e:local            # or: npm run test:e2e (uses these values)
#
# EVERY env var below either targets the suite at a server, or GATES some
# subset of cases. A gated case that is missing its var is skipped, never
# failed — but a skip and a pass render identically in a one-line vitest
# summary, which is exactly how this file went seven weeks without existing on
# this machine, silently disabling every DB-backed case, with the run still
# reporting green the whole time. Two things now make that impossible to miss
# quietly again:
#   1. This file names every gate, which files it gates, and how many cases.
#   2. The gated files themselves print a warning naming the missing var and
#      the exact case count, once per run (src/__tests__/e2e/db-helpers.ts —
#      `envGate` / `announceEnvGates`), so even a mismatched or half-copied
#      `.env.test.local` announces itself in the test output instead of
#      quietly reducing coverage.
#
# If you only came here to make the private-topic / admin-blind cases run,
# you need exactly one var: DATABASE_URL. Everything below E2E_BASE_URL and
# DATABASE_URL is either optional or only relevant to one specific file.

# ─── Target server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required (the suite's global-setup.ts throws immediately if this is unset
# anywhere in the chain — never a silent skip). `npm run test:e2e:local`
# already sets this inline, so you do not strictly need the line below for
# that script; it matters if you invoke vitest directly.
E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3200

# ─── Direct-Postgres gates (the trap this file exists to close) ──────────
#
# Two DIFFERENT var names gate direct-DB e2e cases, and they are easy to
# confuse — that confusion is what caused today's incident, so both are
# spelled out separately rather than as one bullet.
#
# DATABASE_URL — the container's OWN database (same Postgres this local
# `next dev` / Docker container writes to over HTTP). Match your `.env.local`
# DATABASE_URL exactly; if it does not match, direct-DB assertions read an
# unrelated (usually empty) table instead of the rows the HTTP layer just
# created — several of the files below detect and error on that mismatch
# rather than silently passing against the wrong database.
#   Gates, when unset:
#     - src/__tests__/e2e/chat-delivery-purge.test.ts — 6 of 7 numbered cases
#       (the R-1 delivery-purge guard: setting up exact delivery-cursor
#       boundaries needs direct INSERTs no HTTP endpoint exposes)
#     - src/__tests__/e2e/topic-crud.test.ts — cases 13/14 (admin-only
#       `blind` endpoint: promotes a throwaway dev-login user to
#       `users.role='admin'` for the duration via direct UPDATE, then demotes
#       it in a `finally` no matter what — there is no HTTP path to grant
#       admin, so this is the only way to reach that endpoint at all)
#   Does NOT gate (uses the SAME var, but never skips — see below):
#     - src/__tests__/e2e/push-prefs.test.ts (falls back to a hardcoded local
#       default and THROWS if that default is wrong for a non-local target,
#       rather than skipping)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@localhost:5432/openstoa

# E2E_STAGING_DB_URL — historically a Cloud SQL Proxy tunnel to a REMOTE
# deployment (staging), read by src/__tests__/e2e/db-helpers.ts's `hasDb()`.
# Against a local container it points at the exact same database as
# DATABASE_URL above — there is no functional difference locally, only a
# naming one inherited from when this suite only ever ran against staging.
#   Gates, when unset:
#     - src/__tests__/e2e/activity-bump.test.ts — 2 cases (direct-DB proof
#       that a fire-and-forget score/lastActivityAt update actually landed on
#       disk, not just that the API echoed a plausible value)
#     - src/__tests__/e2e/feed.test.ts — 4 cases (pg_trgm GIN index existence
#       + query-plan checks for the search performance guard, migration 0010)
#   Run against real staging instead of local Postgres with:
#     ./scripts/db-proxy.sh staging proxy   # separate terminal
#     E2E_STAGING_DB_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@localhost:15432/openstoa
E2E_STAGING_DB_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@localhost:5432/openstoa

# E2E_DB_URL — push-prefs.test.ts's own preferred name, checked BEFORE
# DATABASE_URL, falling back to the same hardcoded local default as above if
# neither is set (and the target is local). Not itself a second gate — set it
# only if you need push-prefs.test.ts to point somewhere DATABASE_URL should
# not (e.g. verifying dispatch-layer behavior against staging while
# DATABASE_URL still points at your local container for other files).
# E2E_DB_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@localhost:5432/openstoa

# ─── Object storage (media / upload tests) ────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Without it, upload-dependent cases probe the real configured R2
# bucket (via POST /api/upload) and, if credentials are missing, FAIL LOUD
# with a detailed ObjectStorageUnavailable error naming exactly which env vars
# the server itself needs — never a silent skip. Set this only to point media
# assertions at a CDN origin other than what the probe would discover.
# E2E_CDN_ORIGIN=https://media.example.com

# ─── Proof-gated topics (proof-gated-topics.test.ts only) ─────────────────
# Every case in that one file needs a real ZK proof from the zkproofport-prove
# CLI, which needs a live prover and a live OIDC device-code flow. All of the
# following THROW A LOUD, LABELED ERROR when missing or unreachable (see
# ExternalDependencyUnavailable in that file) — never a silent skip. They are
# already set in the committed .env.test (pointing at staging), so you only
# need to override them here if you want a different target.
#   PROOFPORT_URL                — the ZKProofport prover the CLI calls
#   E2E_ATTESTATION_WALLET_KEY   — signing key the CLI uses to submit proofs
#   E2E_GOOGLE_USER_A/B          — Google account hints for the OIDC device flow
#   E2E_MS365_USER_A/B           — Microsoft 365 account hints, same purpose
# PROOFPORT_URL=https://stg-ai.zkproofport.app
# E2E_ATTESTATION_WALLET_KEY=0x...
# E2E_GOOGLE_USER_A=you@example.com
# E2E_GOOGLE_USER_B=you2@example.com
# E2E_MS365_USER_A=you@example.onmicrosoft.com
# E2E_MS365_USER_B=you2@example.onmicrosoft.com

# ─── Auth token cache (auto-managed — you should not normally set these) ──
# global-setup.ts dev-logs-in a fresh User A and writes these itself unless
# already set; helpers.ts throws a clear error if they end up missing. Only
# set them by hand to reuse a specific session across manual runs.
# E2E_AUTH_TOKEN=
# E2E_USER_ID=
